#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171799 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/id #uuid "78a80655-36ca-5628-b11a-4ac492b7cb3e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8938" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u, \\quad \ny=1+u^2, \\quad\nz=v^2\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2.$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: 1 + u^2, \\: v^2\\big\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-4,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171800 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "da389dec-eca9-5f6c-8487-fdcbc0cca227" :question/math-academy-id "e-8939" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/e81d44c7891de67ac97b59abe1bd1c2b67335bb809e3dc5031a6c21b33785eda.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/2a1d8507dddd64183827d51345a244628443cf3ed30f86249131ccb8c1e855ee.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/a7bc8338d348d8e1c18ac970870593c29560ff3c349e31796b62dcd1c35cfcd1.png) lies on the surface, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/d62dba719e321fcd67f78f9ec20b2cffe5fb5ed00d4a2c65392e1520632a1e38.png)\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/5a87223bfdfcf175ccbdd1f94ebd06d92ab9ad841cbb9cf59dab31940fa61c40.png)\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/0d1b1e8a3ef8680d59a924e596e06a0cdccc946ee2cc426527f2de7893f69564.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/00341d0f3526e0407ed756cb16b940e213fb30f762e55370e13006ac8f603f37.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/f4c33acdfdc112d5e252f26cfd33a172fff21f412adbb0071ebcb50f561deaa8.png)\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/c4a233bd69566c25e0aeb6736d21dca4aff73a92015a2831d0d0e8fb0243f7ec.png) is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/722fa4913d73cae67f202a7a25fec74cdad63866bb4297bf8e8058b4808f4c20.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171801 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/id #uuid "a5f4a28a-c56d-5c26-bb55-fd6b8b4424cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-8940" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle v^2, \\: u-v, \\: u^2 \\big\\rangle$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=-1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,-1) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,-1) & =⟨2(-1),\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-8,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=-1$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n\\big( (-1)^2, \\: 2-(-1), \\: 2^2 \\big) = (1, 3, 4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-8,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4\\cdot (x-1)+(-8)\\cdot (y-3)+2\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x-8y+2z+12 & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+z+6 & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+z & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171802 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "b4914ab3-353a-5c74-9126-0358177e2025" :question/math-academy-id "e-8941" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v, \\quad\ny=3u^2, \\quad\nz=u-v\n$$\n\nat the point $(2 ,3, 0).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u+v, \\: 3u^2, \\: u-v \\big\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(2, 3, 0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/9a57281535511312d2fda6f388161fcd624354785d73d48954d10f9e7821653b.png)\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,6(1),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2,\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-6,\\,2,\\,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-6)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-3)+(-6)\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -6x+2y-6z+6 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-3z+3 & =0 \\\\ 3x-y+3z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf9b9227-6a90-5d08-8c54-d3c25854f3ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168128} {:answer/id #uuid "e066f492-305d-5ace-a616-33596f73cfa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-4, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168129} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6268a5-c9c0-5590-bec2-3616e0b61baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168130} {:answer/id #uuid "19e81edf-df1a-5832-b39a-b8c59821ad8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4, 1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168131} {:answer/id #uuid "5b051447-66d5-539d-acd9-a9765d71b420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 4, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6268a5-c9c0-5590-bec2-3616e0b61baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168130} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e2b0a22-f9ad-55e2-bcf0-35f112581707" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eacf6e9-24ec-5d35-b5ca-6a839ae4584e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105544" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y={u}^{2}v,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2.$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}v,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{u}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(1)(2),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,(1)^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c69073d7-a2ba-5855-8f2f-77bff8b593dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x - z = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168140} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a916a4-6e28-5870-8c8d-9b92d83ae20f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 4z = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168141} {:answer/id #uuid "130fb0d2-2d5d-5827-89b8-53ee8ef15015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - z = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168142} {:answer/id #uuid "1857c117-6836-5930-b899-64e2975095ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x + y - 2z = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168143} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad3832f-f829-57a6-985f-7637834455df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x - y - 2z = 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c69073d7-a2ba-5855-8f2f-77bff8b593dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x - z = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168140} :answer-field/id #uuid "96bccc09-c19b-5ebc-858a-4a5c0fa6d730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43478c53-fcac-53e0-adfc-5ae3af04dd56" :question/math-academy-id "q-105594" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4{u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,8u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4{u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,8(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨0,\\,(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,0,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=\\pi $ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(1),\\,(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,4(1)^{2})=(2,0,4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨8,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot (x-2)+0\\cdot y+(-2)\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ 8x-2z-8 & =0 \\\\ 4x-z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e106a44e-856a-50c5-a3ec-ce309dddf598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+2z=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349158} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb0641b-e9f0-5a05-992b-0bf0b3a3a8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349159} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb7364d-ce26-5066-9437-d9018bfa1ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y+2z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349160} {:answer/id #uuid "18f0d7f0-fb41-5937-b5bf-299782fd614b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+4z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349161} {:answer/id #uuid "401ddec7-679c-5e5f-88a5-e9f44863e9a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bb0641b-e9f0-5a05-992b-0bf0b3a3a8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349159} :answer-field/id #uuid "f34c5263-9a9c-58b6-baee-a08adcef71ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2edd9c1d-c147-5e5b-9fc6-73e22654b300" :question/math-academy-id "q-109707" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,u+v,\\,uv⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,1,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨2(1),\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨-2(1),\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=1$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n({1}^{2}-{1}^{2},\\,1+1,\\,1\\cdot 1)=(0,2,1),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,-4,\\,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+(-4)\\cdot (y-2)+4\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -4y+4z+4 & =0 \\\\ -y+z+1 & =0 \\\\ y-z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd4bb3c1-8c1a-5f97-b3dc-86473a44097e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+6z=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349165} {:answer/id #uuid "f60df86b-5faa-5234-96c3-78af08b6c2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3y+z=144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349166} {:answer/id #uuid "7f6fc43a-f0a1-52f2-930b-47a4a291f8b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y+z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349167} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa9c9ed-837d-502e-9d24-a5ba711f0548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y+3z=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349168} {:answer/id #uuid "1511ce9d-53f0-5120-ac14-47f858f17b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-y+3z=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd4bb3c1-8c1a-5f97-b3dc-86473a44097e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+6z=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349165} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e85a39-47db-5aab-ba74-3c51b40480b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30d022b4-bd01-5a1d-b671-65013c352e27" :question/math-academy-id "q-109760" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2{u}^{3},\\,u{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2uv,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨6(1)^{2},\\,{3}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,9,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)(3),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,3)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,-12,\\,36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=3$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(1)^{3},\\,1(3)^{2},\\,2(3))=(2,9,6),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨18,\\,-12,\\,36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-9,\\,z-6⟩ & =0 \\\\ 18\\cdot (x-2)-12\\cdot (y-9)+36\\cdot (z-6) & =0 \\\\ 18x-12y+36z-144 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z-24 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a198ec01-3b6f-5275-ae90-8098b1713a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-y-2z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349172} {:answer/id #uuid "7b487f7f-ed44-53d6-a46f-6395cacbcfac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349173} {:answer/id #uuid "0e8c2b95-8789-5ef1-b91e-a75ba8ad3ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-2y-z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349174} {:answer/id #uuid "ef2740f1-da2d-5068-bd6d-e7ef2cfee60b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-3y+2z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349175} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec25d03-6f37-5fb5-ada2-828d4e6f092b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e8c2b95-8789-5ef1-b91e-a75ba8ad3ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-2y-z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349174} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc7ef5e3-5f25-503a-a740-71a9ee10b61b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b685693-c3f8-506c-b0f7-15960f52a051" :question/math-academy-id "q-109766" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,{u}^{3}-uv⟩$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=6.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}-uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3{u}^{2}-v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}-uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,6) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3(2)^{2}-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,6⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,6) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,6)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,6) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=6$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2,\\,6,\\,{2}^{3}-(2)(6))=(2,6,-4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-6,\\,2,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-6,\\,z+4⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-6)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-6)+1\\cdot (z+4) & =0 \\\\ -6x+2y+z+4 & =0 \\\\ 6x-2y-z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db426f25-dc49-51af-90ed-31e6dd60a164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y+z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349179} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb86c3e-e602-50ac-9a4c-008ba76ccc9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349180} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ba6a55-b41c-5487-96e2-587aa66f3bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349181} {:answer/id #uuid "e365557a-7255-53cf-b3e1-e6d7b6915b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349182} {:answer/id #uuid "0fecaca7-c140-5481-9193-51644c146320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-2z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e365557a-7255-53cf-b3e1-e6d7b6915b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349182} :answer-field/id #uuid "2560ed49-f93f-5fa9-9726-231ca5752b3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89222e89-ffbe-5ee3-bac2-f4a6a41f3081" :question/math-academy-id "q-109768" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2)=(0,2,2),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-2,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot (y-2)+2\\cdot (z-2) & =0 \\\\ -2y+2z & =0 \\\\ y-z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcf86eac-731c-5887-afab-ac06412a816e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+z=\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349186} {:answer/id #uuid "7723b76d-7ac1-52be-af22-2c7a5f01ee05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y-z=2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349187} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0b491e-26a1-5503-8c08-db33cd2bd3be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+z=\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349188} {:answer/id #uuid "20c447ec-1fef-5651-acd8-f24779e600f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-z=-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349189} {:answer/id #uuid "67314a06-852b-5972-b785-d25b2a5de96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+2z=2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67314a06-852b-5972-b785-d25b2a5de96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+2z=2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349190} :answer-field/id #uuid "55481cdc-3eb1-505e-b7c9-8c58c3f909b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "869764b1-b39c-5501-a85f-79cb4775f065" :question/math-academy-id "q-109813" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point $(-2,0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(-2,0,\\pi )$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-2 \\\\ u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=0 \\\\ v=\\pi \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=2$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\pi ) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y,\\,z-\\pi ⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot (x+2)+1\\cdot y+2\\cdot (z-\\pi ) & =0 \\\\ y+2z-2\\pi  & =0 \\\\ y+2z & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b24d4144-0a84-5e87-b942-9d8eaf4d2d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349193} {:answer/id #uuid "b70caa77-3dc9-51e1-a1ac-f5ab7a5b955d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349194} {:answer/id #uuid "88ca2009-9f5a-53eb-bb51-4051d7c8f8c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349195} {:answer/id #uuid "10055f7f-6154-54a0-805d-2749656af34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349196} {:answer/id #uuid "6c436cc7-a769-501f-8715-801d70a0a2ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c436cc7-a769-501f-8715-801d70a0a2ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349197} :answer-field/id #uuid "c73d6383-5b6b-51a7-917a-633b8485a278" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eb2b5317-b832-5fce-951c-eb11f15634c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-109815" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,z=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nat the point $(1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(1,0,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=0 \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨2(1),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,0)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,0,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-1)+0\\cdot y+4\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -2x+4z-2 & =0 \\\\ -x+2z-1 & =0 \\\\ x-2z & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd883092-69a2-5c5d-9ee5-d54530416645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 4y + 2z = 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168344} {:answer/id #uuid "3112acf2-1315-543c-96f4-ee752b4221bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 4y - 4z =-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168345} {:answer/id #uuid "32a36ae4-5e6f-5884-826b-808aa4535210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + y = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168346} {:answer/id #uuid "4da2fd22-c932-5f1a-b059-95595bb2c20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + y - 2z =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168347} {:answer/id #uuid "51fcca6c-d922-5a02-891e-13caa013126d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 2y = 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3112acf2-1315-543c-96f4-ee752b4221bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 4y - 4z =-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168345} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1fbbf4d-3dc1-5890-801b-84dbbb44d799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5267351-988e-5a64-a5a4-1a3cc67629e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-109818" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nat the point $(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(4,1,4)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=4 \\\\ {v}^{2}=1 \\\\ u+2v=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=2$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨2(2),\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨0,\\,2(1),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-1,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-4)+(-8)\\cdot (y-1)+8\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ -2x-8y+8z-16 & =0 \\\\ -x-4y+4z-8 & =0 \\\\ x+4y-4z & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e00850-1e65-5871-9dc1-424184d621d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+y-4z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349200} {:answer/id #uuid "77c3e560-0d0f-57d9-a58b-60bd8da7466f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349201} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dba2c2-a935-5d83-9aef-23914a7fa5ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y+z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349202} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfa9796-41b9-5723-93eb-14ab0ec40e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2y-3z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349203} {:answer/id #uuid "af4e12dc-0433-5748-ac8d-6e52757922b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0e00850-1e65-5871-9dc1-424184d621d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+y-4z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349200} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f285ac0-213d-54b1-af57-3c3a51e104df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6d931731-94c9-5a44-8fc9-ccd1b9a0a8bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109829" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=uv,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,v\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nat the point $(1,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,uv⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(1,4,2)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=1 \\\\ {v}^{2}=4 \\\\ uv=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨2(1),\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨0,\\,2(2),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,-2,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,\\,-2,\\,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-4,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (x-1)+(-2)\\cdot (y-4)+8\\cdot (z-2) & =0 \\\\ -8x-2y+8z & =0 \\\\ 4x+y-4z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76d7926a-c174-527a-887d-ddaee8d0f2b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349207} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3b1cb7-9aeb-5ebf-a4cd-5660f6844cf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-2z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349208} {:answer/id #uuid "d4290ba0-8115-5d93-b507-b60ee52a8dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349209} {:answer/id #uuid "bde0cdf9-da9f-5e13-83c0-58e0ea00b025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y-2z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349210} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8efd7e-90fd-5b54-ae40-0c778847c8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76d7926a-c174-527a-887d-ddaee8d0f2b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349207} :answer-field/id #uuid "e15f4300-69a8-57a6-ab06-531a187b9a77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3675d541-d23c-5142-93bd-432d63bfa009" :question/math-academy-id "q-109831" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,y={u}^{2},\\,z=2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nat the point $(0,1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(0,1,-2)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=0 \\\\ {u}^{2}=1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0,\\,-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,2(1),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨1\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,0,\\,-2(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-1,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+2\\cdot (y-1)+2\\cdot (z+2) & =0 \\\\ 2y+2z+2 & =0 \\\\ y+z & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b20e130-0b0d-5d20-be8b-e2bef49747c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,1,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349214} {:answer/id #uuid "995e007a-8e74-5c51-8ed2-ebb765ed762e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349215} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0b37e1-0411-54d6-9b0d-366c83dd9699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349216} {:answer/id #uuid "13af0280-1117-5e3f-8a19-5bf4aace01a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349217} {:answer/id #uuid "251bd744-6406-5990-9bc3-769277b0fc5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13af0280-1117-5e3f-8a19-5bf4aace01a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c898d39-a5b9-5aff-8e7e-be6c5ea68a32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bc3a57c-16b1-5e15-a995-b394c905acdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-109842" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2u+v,\\,y={u}^{2},\\,z={v}^{2}\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\,{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨2,\\,2(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e74ab5d6-ec08-50f1-b60b-cf42d884ba0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349221} {:answer/id #uuid "435e1510-187a-5f41-963e-d56786157624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349222} {:answer/id #uuid "ff46c298-e1f6-54af-b1e6-98983b09961b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,4,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349223} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fb2173-224d-578d-a04f-2eb4924b7e13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,0,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349224} {:answer/id #uuid "bf41e25e-986d-5e9b-b2d3-0a7a61e87423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e74ab5d6-ec08-50f1-b60b-cf42d884ba0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349221} :answer-field/id #uuid "117d3915-0aaf-5100-8f66-5836195e56e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c70bbed7-d1c1-590a-80d6-f3c67f5ba6af" :question/math-academy-id "q-109884" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={v}^{2},\\,y=2v,\\,z=4u\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{v}^{2},\\,2v,\\,4u⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨2(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,4,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a933b2ee-7e20-5228-893c-08afc72ab3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0, 2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168350} {:answer/id #uuid "fa83163b-860f-5da1-9709-f65b1e160bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168351} {:answer/id #uuid "fb08a828-3dc3-5cb8-85e0-0458f9278644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168352} {:answer/id #uuid "67ab78d6-29a5-55cc-89f7-7ded0070166f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168353} {:answer/id #uuid "6833020a-95a8-532f-9e3a-814fa49d54a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0, 1, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb08a828-3dc3-5cb8-85e0-0458f9278644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168352} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f8de470-fa2f-503c-ac2b-47b070bc5762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d781e9d-2506-5e3b-a6d2-c89a045be30c" :question/math-academy-id "q-109888" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u,\\,z=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0,\\,1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd082b0-c538-59e4-93ef-5010fcc8458e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349228} {:answer/id #uuid "62e170bb-b7d5-53ff-a2d2-3d5d7290fa36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,2e,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349229} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7a58c5-6809-5e1f-a254-5ba4238abb7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,e,\\,-e⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349230} {:answer/id #uuid "1286713c-7f9b-5daf-a3b9-fb18c949f537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{2},\\,{e}^{-1},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349231} {:answer/id #uuid "5c227330-0a43-55b4-8dc8-d57805452bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,2e⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd082b0-c538-59e4-93ef-5010fcc8458e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349228} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba17f9c-242f-546a-90d0-f22c9c9cf59e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50079234-7f4e-52ec-a92b-b77c984bf96b" :question/math-academy-id "q-109894" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=1+{e}^{u},\\,y=2-{e}^{v},\\,z=1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v}\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨1+{e}^{u},\\,2-{e}^{v},\\,1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+{e}^{u}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{u},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{u}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+{e}^{u}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,-{e}^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨{e}^{1},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨e,\\,0,\\,-e⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨0,\\,-{e}^{-1},\\,-{e}^{-1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ e & 0 & -e \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-1} & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -e \\\\ -{e}^{-1} & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}e & -e \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}e & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dce7e1d-1910-526d-8560-6da758f55bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349235} {:answer/id #uuid "871b08cd-c5c1-5405-bbdb-ecc4f72288bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,0,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349236} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6587ce-5b81-50ca-8f55-e4c3deb13855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349237} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e0d097-4267-5b70-8af8-cd30d6f42239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349238} {:answer/id #uuid "37533cb5-5bb6-5620-a1f5-d1cf89e28af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37533cb5-5bb6-5620-a1f5-d1cf89e28af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349239} :answer-field/id #uuid "3759a5a1-120f-54f8-8964-7140144287ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "300c83ab-2970-5bf8-a21f-eb8cc4e48489" :question/math-academy-id "q-109929" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨1+v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}⟩$ at the point $(2,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(2,1,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1+v=2 \\\\ uv=1 \\\\ {u}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,v,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,u,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(2,1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3941cb6b-7d7b-5177-8460-2ac8aa4f0c0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,4,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349242} {:answer/id #uuid "05055d44-309c-51ce-89a7-43fa2801f3fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349243} {:answer/id #uuid "31216c2d-5930-5125-a185-0407018d6d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349244} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6b638e-124b-5e13-b386-3b07b6d67c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349245} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d9c0be-ec71-5233-b2ff-848fa5b8de78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2d9c0be-ec71-5233-b2ff-848fa5b8de78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349246} :answer-field/id #uuid "25a8684f-e237-5bd6-a63d-f93f55c59e11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b66f3f39-0aab-5d32-a8a6-87d4d0a13cbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-109930" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨1+u,\\,2v,\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}⟩$ at the point $(2,-4,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(2,-4,-3)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1+u=2 \\\\ 2v=-4 \\\\ {u}^{2}-{v}^{2}=-3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,-2) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-2) & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(2,-4,-3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf83305f-b413-522e-b3dd-21b6fb3575ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349249} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9d6ca1-8910-5b5a-bb6c-ca8e3d6bc720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349250} {:answer/id #uuid "3bff766f-9fda-5a4b-8aaf-80b03b3656f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349251} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4d07f4-75dd-51c5-878b-3e58c58a0ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349252} {:answer/id #uuid "e67f491d-cbe0-5d68-ac7e-b94738480d81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d4d07f4-75dd-51c5-878b-3e58c58a0ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349252} :answer-field/id #uuid "58bec858-6b94-5ae2-9d48-eb20fcaaa571" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0b584d0-a4fc-5d30-8371-8557a5098ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-110060" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-v⟩$ at the point $(1,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(1,1,2)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ {v}^{2}=1 \\\\ {u}^{2}-v=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨0,\\,2(-1),\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9055d350-a1ec-5cc5-9277-ca29d89e4aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,4,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349256} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a6113-0858-591f-b383-2adfea20e108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349257} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2933f4-d09a-58d3-9026-fafcc51df1eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,2,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349258} {:answer/id #uuid "39edf203-49be-571e-bdd2-1b2ec46c6b9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349259} {:answer/id #uuid "02cc26b8-a9fd-5b17-a6c3-96a41357b2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9055d350-a1ec-5cc5-9277-ca29d89e4aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,4,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349256} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b7d54e7-39cc-5f8e-95aa-6734b4010a7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c0c66a10-3373-58d2-b295-e418ae85a482" :question/math-academy-id "q-110070" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u,\\,(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\n at the point $(1,1,\\sqrt{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(2,3,4)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=1 \\\\ u=1 \\\\ (1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,1,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0,\\,-(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =⟨2(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}),\\,1,\\,2(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =⟨(1+(1)^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}),\\,0,\\,-(1+(1)^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,\\sqrt{3})$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,4,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "498f1356-e007-5363-8785-18fcf96e251c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349263} {:answer/id #uuid "3e52d551-93bd-5f25-a8c5-8e3f526872dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,-4,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349264} {:answer/id #uuid "37bc2f99-d60d-5905-913b-8802b4c8fcf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349265} {:answer/id #uuid "741c91b6-fa30-5385-81e7-d6fff22e2473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-1,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349266} {:answer/id #uuid "4331e8e7-1bac-5d03-b594-dc0238e7fc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4331e8e7-1bac-5d03-b594-dc0238e7fc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349267} :answer-field/id #uuid "3807ecfc-47bd-5b80-9f4e-6badada461bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3ec2996-8134-58a4-92f7-407bb32b0c97" :question/math-academy-id "q-110546" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,v⟩$ at the point $(1,2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(1,2,0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u+v=1 \\\\ 2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}=2 \\\\ v=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨1,\\,4(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨1,\\,2(0),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,2,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,0)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
